+// [netplay] Online play for two players by input lockstep.
+//
+// MODEL: the two games never exchange game state, only the pads. With PS2X_DETERMINISTIC=1 a game is a function of its
+// pad inputs (and PS2X_RTC, and its memory card), so two machines that feed the same inputs on the same frames run the
+// same game. Both boot on their own and meet at the first vblank: from there each frame is numbered by the vblank
+// count, which is the same on both.
+//
+// TIMING: the input sampled at vblank F is applied at vblank F + delay, which gives the network delay * 16.7 ms to
+// carry it. A game that does not have the other player's input for the frame waits for it (lockstep). Each packet
+// repeats the last kRedundancy inputs, so a lost datagram heals with the next one: UDP, no retransmits.
+//
+// CHECK: every PS2X_NET_CHECKEVERY frames (60) both hash all of EE RAM at the vblank and compare: a difference is a
+// desync, logged with its frame.
+//
+//   PS2X_NET_PLAYER=1|2                 which player is local (1 = port 1, 2 = port 2)
+//   PS2X_NET_RELAY=<host:port> PS2X_NET_TOKEN=<32 hex>   through the online server's relay (RLY1, see server/relay.go)
+//   PS2X_NET=<host:port> / PS2X_NET_LISTEN=<port>        direct, for tests on one machine or a LAN
+//   PS2X_NET_DELAY=<frames>|auto        input delay (auto: player 1 measures the round trip and tells player 2)
+//   PS2X_NET_WAIT_MS=<ms>               how long to wait for the other player at the start (default 60000)
+//   PS2X_NET_TIMEOUT=<ms>               silence that ends the match during play (default 10000)
+//   PS2X_NET_STATUS_FILE=<path>         "online" once both play, "offline <why>" when the match ends (the launcher)
+
+#include "NetPlay.h"
+
